        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mill_spring_north_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Mill Spring sits in the Blue Ridge foothills at 1,001 feet, 35°17′51″N 82°09′40″W.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mill_spring_north_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1767 Governor William Tryon negotiated a treaty with Cherokee, setting a boundary that included Mill Spring.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mill_spring_north_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1925 Turner Shoals Dam created a 371‑acre reservoir that now serves as a sediment trap and recreation spot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
